---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import CTA from "../components/CTA.astro";
import Schema from "../components/Schema.astro";
import SectionHeader from "../components/SectionHeader.astro";
import { offers, pillars, people, bookHighlights, seoOpportunities } from "../lib/site";
---
<Base title="Kingdom Factor" description="A trusted advisory circle for Christian business owners who want to lead with wisdom, faith, and accountability.">
  <Schema />
  <section class="home-hero polished-hero executive-hero editorial-hero">
    <div class="hero-copy editorial-hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Private counsel for Christian CEOs, owners, and senior leaders</p>
      <h1>Ensure you're in the room where wisdom surrounds you.</h1>
      <p>Kingdom Factor helps faith-driven owners process high-stakes decisions with qualified peers, seasoned coaching, and biblical wisdom around growth, culture, stewardship, and leadership pressure.</p>
      <div class="actions hero-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/apply/">Request a fit conversation</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/peer-advisory-groups/">See the advisory path</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="decision-room-section" aria-label="Kingdom Factor advisory setting">
    <div class="decision-room-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">What changes in the room</p>
      <h2>The conversation moves from encouragement to judgment, counsel, and action.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="decision-room-lines">
      <p><strong>Isolation gets named.</strong> Owners can speak plainly about decisions that affect people, money, culture, family, faith, and the future of the business.</p>
      <p><strong>Blind spots get challenged.</strong> Qualified peers and seasoned advisors help pressure-test the next move before it becomes expensive.</p>
      <p><strong>Stewardship becomes practical.</strong> The point is not inspiration. The point is wiser decisions, faithful execution, and clear next steps.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="council-model-section model-section">
    <div class="council-model-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">The Kingdom Factor model</p>
      <h2>Three lanes, one purpose: do not lead alone.</h2>
      <p>Peer advisory, private coaching, and marketplace ministry form a practical path from owner isolation into qualified counsel.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="council-model-list">
      {pillars.map((pillar, index) => (
        <article class="council-lane">
          <span>0{index + 1}</span>
          <div>
            <h3>{pillar.title}</h3>
            <p>{pillar.text}</p>
          </div>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="paths" class="lane-section">
    <SectionHeader eyebrow="Choose your path" title="Built for established executives and emerging owners in different seasons." text="The right next step depends on the weight of your decisions, the maturity of your business, and the kind of counsel you need now." align="center" />
    <div class="lane-grid">
      {people.map((person) => (
        <article class={`lane-card leader-lane ${person.lane === "Executive advisory" ? "executive" : "community"}`}>
          <img class="leader-portrait" src={person.image} alt={person.name} loading="lazy" />
          <p class="eyebrow">{person.lane}</p>
          <h3>{person.name}</h3>
          <p><strong>{person.role}</strong></p>
          <p>{person.summary}</p>
          <a class="text-link" href={person.href}>Explore this pathway →</a>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="offer-section pathway-section">
    <SectionHeader eyebrow="Offer ecosystem" title="Move from curiosity to a qualified conversation." text="Resources and preview paths help leaders understand the model before they request a fit conversation or apply for a room." align="center" />
    <div class="offer-grid pathway-grid">
      {offers.map((offer) => (
        <article class="offer-card premium-card">
          <p>{offer.audience}</p>
          <h3>{offer.title}</h3>
          <p>{offer.summary}</p>
          <a href={offer.href}>View pathway →</a>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="authority-section">
    <div class="authority-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Authority layer</p>
      <h2>Books, webinars, and leadership IP should build trust before the first call.</h2>
      <p>Kingdom Factor can use John and Jim’s resource library to answer the questions Christian owners already carry about accountability, marketplace ministry, leadership development, and faithful execution.</p>
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/books/">View books and resources</a>
    </div>
    <div class="image-feature-card motion-card">
      <picture>
        <source media="(max-width: 640px)" srcset="/images/generated/leadership-table-mobile.webp" />
        <img src="/images/generated/leadership-table-1440.webp" alt="Leadership table with warm executive counsel materials" loading="lazy" />
      </picture>
      <div class="book-cloud overlay-cloud">
        {bookHighlights.slice(0, 6).map((book) => <span>{book}</span>)}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="seo-section">
    <SectionHeader eyebrow="Leadership topics" title="Built around the questions Christian owners are already carrying." text="The resource path can grow into practical guides for faith-and-business leadership, peer counsel, accountability, and stewardship." align="center" />
    <div class="keyword-grid">
      {seoOpportunities.map((keyword) => <span>{keyword}</span>)}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="source-section story-section">
    <div class="source-panel story-panel">
      <p class="eyebrow">Kingdom Factor Collective</p>
      <h2>Real stories help leaders see faithful business in practice.</h2>
      <p>The Collective gives Christian owners a place to learn from grounded conversations about calling, courage, stewardship, culture, and the decisions leaders rarely process alone.</p>
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/collective/">Explore leadership stories</a>
    </div>
    <div class="story-list" aria-label="Kingdom Factor story themes">
      <article>
        <span>01</span>
        <h3>Faith in business</h3>
        <p>Conversations about integrating conviction into decisions, culture, people, and growth.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>02</span>
        <h3>Leadership under pressure</h3>
        <p>Stories for owners carrying risk, responsibility, conflict, and stewardship.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>03</span>
        <h3>Marketplace ministry</h3>
        <p>Practical examples of serving people well while building a healthy business.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="faq-section closing-faq" aria-labelledby="homepage-faq-title">
    <div class="faq-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Questions before a fit conversation</p>
      <h2 id="homepage-faq-title">A few things Christian owners usually ask first.</h2>
      <p>Serious leaders can get clear context without pressure. These questions explain who the rooms are for, how the paths differ, and what a fit conversation is meant to clarify.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list compact-faq">
      <details open>
        <summary>Who is Kingdom Factor designed for?</summary>
        <p>Christian CEOs, business owners, senior executives, founders, and emerging owners who want qualified counsel around decisions that affect business performance, people, stewardship, and faith.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is this coaching, peer advisory, or ministry?</summary>
        <p>It can be any of those paths depending on the leader. The fit conversation helps determine whether peer advisory, private executive coaching, marketplace ministry resources, or a lighter community path is most appropriate.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What happens after I request a fit conversation?</summary>
        <p>The goal is discernment, not pressure. Kingdom Factor can learn what kind of decisions you are carrying, explain the available rooms, and recommend the next step only if there is a real fit.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Are the groups confidential?</summary>
        <p>Confidentiality is treated as a core expectation for serious peer counsel. Fit conversations can clarify the room structure, membership criteria, and operating details before anyone joins.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTA title="Next step" text="Find the right path for the season you are leading through. Start with a fit conversation. We will help you discern whether to begin with a peer advisory group, engage in executive coaching, explore marketplace ministry resources, or pursue a strategic combination of these options to move you toward your goals." />
</Base>
